 the fix — the buggy code crashes with `IndexOutOfBoundsException` on `\"=\".split(\"=\")`, while the fixed code with `split(\"=\", 2)` handles all edge cases correctly without any exceptions.\n\n### Build Note\nThe Android build (`./gradlew clean assembleDebug`) cannot complete in this environment due to network restrictions preventing download of the Android Gradle Plugin 8.3.0 from Google's Maven repository. The code change itself is syntactically correct and follows the existing project patterns.","usage":{"input_tokens":755041,"output_tokens":7600,"cache_read_input_tokens":704256,"total_tokens":762641},"permission_denials":[]}
